column4:
Hello! I haven’t been making much art lately, but I’m finding my way back to my creative practice. Here’s a little about my background and what I’m working on:

//
Marshall Wang Meixuan (b. 1999, Shenzhen) is a Chinese graphic designer and art director based in Brooklyn, New York. Her practice spans moving image, installation, publishing, interaction design, creative technology, and visual systems. Working across aesthetics, simulacra, networked media, and identity, she creates synthetic yet intimate experiences that examine post-digital culture, technological infrastructure, and the politics of imagery.

Marshall holds an MFA in Design and Technology from Parsons School of Design and a BFA in Graphic Design from California Institute of the Arts. Her work has been exhibited or presented at Pioneer Works, Recess, Flowing Space, IIDRR Gallery, Boston Cyberarts Gallery, MIT Media Lab, CultureHub / La MaMa, and the National Gallery of Denmark. She is the co-founder of Sequence Giftshop, an artist collective exploring gestures of care through independent publishing and object making.

//
I’m currently working on an ongoing project, Prayer on the Internet, which takes the form of a publication. I’d like to develop it into an installation, exploring how its imagery might translate into a spatial experience. The exact form is still open, but I envision an image-driven, screen-based work.
